WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.900
Tama-chan!

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.300
School is pretty far, so we need to leave soon!

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.370
Wait up!

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.460
Sorry ahm late.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.480
What's wrong, Yumine?

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.340
This is no good! Redo it.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:27.920
Eh?

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.740
Tama-chan, we're in high school now, you know?

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.580
And what's with this baggy uniform?

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.680
Grandma said a'm goin' ta grow up fast, so she bought me one a size too big...

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.880
Also, no dialect, use standard Japanese.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.850
No way!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.650
I-I understand.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.870
Our uniforms really are expensive though.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.400
I've been going to this school since middle school,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.770
but you lived in the countryside, so it might be difficult for you.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.880
Our house ain't that far out!

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.680
See, there's your accent again.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.120
Yeah.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.310
I'm Honda Tamaki.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.450
The entrance ceremony is today.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.450
I'm going to Hoshinotsuji private high school.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.340
It's famous for its lively club activities, stemming from its tradition of freedom.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.640
Today, after the entrance ceremony,

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.850
you can visit clubs and see their displays during an event called club PR.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.110
The school is in the center of town.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.740
It's completely different to my middle school, so it'll take some time to get used to.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.450
Look, we're here, Tama-chan.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
The Start Line

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.020
After the entrance ceremony and homeroom,

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.280
the new students are allowed to freely look around during club PR.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.900
I've been looking forward to this day, when I would enter a wonderful club, however...

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:55.520
I still don't know what activities I can be passionate about.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.880
Our first club PR, huh?

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.540
I wonder what kind of new students will join.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.450
It's your shift at the DTM's club display soon, right, Fujikawa-san?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.200
Yeah, that's true. But this is important too.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.890
It would be great if we got someone who can draw.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.100
Oh! If we got someone who wants to be a voice actor, that would be fun.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.170
It won't be easy to get someone good.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.980
By the way, why don't you put these on?

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.280
Only the president can wear those.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.280
That's not right, starting today our president is...

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:29.980
You're right.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.970
I'm done. Let's hurry.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.210
Good luck, new president.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.220
This school has a lot of clubs, huh?

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.510
I wanted to see more, but it's already so late.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:47.640
I understand. It's easy to establish a new club here.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.300
Wow! This matcha tastes good.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.770
I'm glad.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.640
It's really good.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.190
Yahoo, Tama-chan!

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.370
Yumine!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.220
How was it, did you decide on a club?

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:08.800
Not yet. There are so many, and I end up talking for a long time.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:09.910
Oh dear.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.880
I joined the Illustration Club.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.910
So they also have a club like that.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.800
Is there some kind of club you want to join?

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.800
Hmm... I wonder...

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:25.810
I wonder if I can find my true calling, a club that I'll feel I have to join.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.040
It's easier to do something than to worry about it, you know.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.200
But still,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:34.850
Hm?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.690
there sure are a lot of kinds of clubs.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.880
Aya, their young smiles are so bright.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.360
Shii, calm down. I'm deeply regretful for making you pull an all nighter.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.960
Um, what club is this?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.000
Uh, um...

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:58.910
Our club creates doujin games. You can play the game we created if you like.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.200
Doujin?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.760
You make your own games?

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.090
That's amazing!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.880
Doujin games?

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.920
They are quite simplistic though.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.520
The promotional video is currently playing on this computer.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:14.980
The PC is frozen!

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.370
Ah, I'm so sorry! I'll restart it!

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.020
Shii, your tea! You'll get wet!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.310
Please don't panic!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.230
So it's a puzzle game.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.850
Wow, the art is really cute.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.700
Can we play it?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.020
Please do.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.200
I'm so nervous. Maybe I should step away for a bit.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.740
Um, let's see. It's the character selection. You can pick first Tama-chan.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:38.280
Thanks, Yumine.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:43.230
So cute! I've gotten a spark of inspiration for my next scenario!

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.500
Don't show them that vulgar smile.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.140
Ah! We're already battling an enemy.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.340
But it's showing us the instructions.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.840
<i>I wonder if they'll understand the tutorial. Please don't let there be any bugs.</i>

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.080
The controls are quite tricky.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.060
It really makes you think hard.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.940
These kittens are enchanted by my scenario!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.580
This is puzzle game though.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.800
We finally beat it.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.260
That was exciting! It's exhilarating when you finally beat them.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.340
So cute. New students are great, aren't they?

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:21.300
Shii-san, your tone suddenly changed, but you're right, they are.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.570
Oh no, we're out of time. I thought we were just about to beat it.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:32.190
Geez, if only I'd made fewer mistakes.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:35.400
I-I'm sorry, we got really into it.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.400
No, it's fine. It makes me glad that we made it.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.880
It's quite well made.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.200
I wouldn't have thought it was made by club.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.600
Thank you very much.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:48.110
Really! It's just like the Hoyofuyo game I got when I was kid.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:52.800
It reminds me of when I got addicted to it. You based it off that game, right?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.280
You're right. We used the common mechanics from action-puzzle games as a base,

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.140
so even if you cover it up with presentation, no wonder... and I knew it in the back of my mind.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.250
Shii, calm down!

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.800
Did I say something weird?

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.320
Oh... is this something you made together?

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.920
Yes, there were two other members, though.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.620
Here's the case art.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.380
How do you make a game?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.600
You create the art, story, and music on a computer.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.200
And you assemble them into a game.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:31.040
Everyone is constructing a game world together, in a sense.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.200
It's really interesting.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.000
So you use a computer?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.140
I draw too, but I haven't done much digital art.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.620
That's fine, you can take your time to learn it now.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.580
It's hard.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.450
Huh?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:43.920
Um...

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.180
It's hard.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:57.040
I'm very sorry, but I don't think I can join. I'll have my hands full with the Illustration Club.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.640
What about you Tama-chan? You used to draw a lot.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:06.450
I only drew a bit in elementary school. And I don't really know how to draw using a computer.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.800
I don't think I can create something good enough to use in a game.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.920
You don't have to worry so much.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.900
She seems to have a very earnest expression.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.080
We'll be on our way then.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.400
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.310
The new students were really cute.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:31.140
Yeah, they really were.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:34.110
Ah, the time for club PR is over.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:38.370
I think I'll join the Tea Ceremony Club. They were nice, after all.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.850
Why don't you join the Illustration Club with me?

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.640
I went earlier, it seems like we could just draw in a laid-back atmosphere.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:47.460
Yeah...

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.900
That game was really fun. It was cute and sparkly.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:59.420
They're all so focused on making games. I don't have anything like that.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.420
To begin with, what is it I want to do?

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:07.520
I was really into card games, so I studied single-player ones.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.880
I read old books by the river while looking at the clouds.

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.570
I tried copying the art from manga.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:18.020
I shut myself up in the closet and got engrossed in manga.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:23.220
I tried to draw the funniest thing I could in my textbooks.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.140
I caught bugs and studied them on the porch.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:32.510
There's no consistency in my hobbies. Just what is it I want to do.

00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:33.380
Hey!

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.220
Grandma, look, look!

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.880
You made a board game today?

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.620
Tamaki is so good at thinking up games.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.840
When I become an elementary schooler, I'll make a bunch of games with my friends!

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:56.180
You're a good girl, so I think you can do it. I'm sure you'll make a lot of them.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:05.020
That's right. The reason I became friends with Yumine was also...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.020
Today, I made a new game!

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.000
Wow!

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:12.980
Hey!

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.960
Hey, Tama-chan!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:20.450
To think up games, could this be...

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.650
Why are you spacing out?

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:25.200
Sorry, Yumine, go on without me.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.200
Tama-chan?!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.000
There you are.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.760
Oh! A first year?

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.500
Um...

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.140
I'm Fujikawa, a second year club member.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.480
I was in charge of the music for this puzzle game.

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:42.300
Did you get a chance to play it?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.220
The music?

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.840
I was too into the game, so I didn't really notice...

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:55.480
I-I see. Of course you didn't, the background music shouldn't stand out much.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.210
No one says the bass line was great,

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.850
There's no one who comments like that.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.510
I'm sorry, I've said too much again.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:08.500
I'm only joking, for you not to have noticed it means that it's actually a great success for me.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.710
So, why did you come back?

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:17.920
Um, I thought the art was really nice, and I'm a bit interested in making games.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:24.220
I don't know if I can do it, but if I could learn from the person who drew this,

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.620
I think that even I could.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.770
She's no longer here.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.850
Huh?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.250
She created this club one year ago, you see.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:39.820
She was able to pull us along to create this puzzle game as our first work.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:44.250
She was an amazing person who did the art, planning, and management all by herself.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.180
But she's already graduated.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:52.570
So, the club is now just us three. We don't have an artist, or even a leader.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.960
We're at the point where we just don't know what to do.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.960
You don't have someone who can draw?

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.590
That's why we had high hopes for the new students.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.340
But in the end, no one joined.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.200
It's only the first day of the new term. We're just getting started!

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.050
I will...

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.060
Huh?

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.520
I will join your club!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.460
By all means!

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.620
I'll do my best to learn to use computers!

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.800
I see, I'm glad to hear it! Thank you!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.030
You've drawn before? Like illustrations?

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:35.200
I've only tried copying manga, but, if you'll have me, I'd like to try creating games.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.040
We'll welcome you with open arms!

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.250
Why don't you try drawing something.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:45.380
That's her art style?!

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:50.760
Are there any weird parts with my rough sketch? It's been a while since I've drawn.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:56.340
Ah, um... I think it's really good.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.940
Thank you.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:03.060
I'm Honda Tamaki. I'm going to give making games my all.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:13.710
Tama-chan, you ended up joining that game club?

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:19.210
Yeah, they didn't have anyone who could draw, so I said I would join if they would take me.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.560
How brave.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.840
Today they're holding a club meeting.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:26.220
I wonder what you do at a game-making meeting.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.940
That seems kinda cool.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.970
Are you going to the Illustration Club, Yumine?

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.140
Yeah. Today we're doing introductions.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:35.480
It's really exciting to show others your art, isn't it?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:42.140
That's true too, but there was a pretty senpai who drank out of this slightly cute guy's cup.

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:45.940
His reaction to that also made me really excited.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.490
Hm?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.940
Shii! This is finally the long awaited day for our club!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.200
Hey! You're already doing that?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.120
They were selling a new flavor.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:00.880
By combining two ordinary drinks, I can enjoy a small amount of chaos.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:01.400
Pudding Lemonade

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:01.400
Matcha

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.310
Don't you think that's a fun way to get rid of boredom?

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.510
Sure, just make sure you drink that.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:16.020
Okay, please introduce yourself, new student.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.970
Y-Yes! First year, Honda Tamaki.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.940
I don't have any experience making games or drawing, but it's nice to meet you!

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:30.000
U-um... here. My grandmother said I should bring something when making a new home.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.520
Oh.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.400
How is it?

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:35.200
It's good.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.530
These are tasty.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.830
It's seasoned well. This is good kinpira.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:47.280
It's good, but is that really what you do as a club?

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.720
Anyway, we're glad to have you.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:50.840
You're up next, President.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.850
I'm Murakami Shiina, I'm a second year student and the programmer.

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.710
President, I look forward to working with you.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:59.740
I feel like I just joined in the heat of the moment.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.850
That's fine, that passion is important for creating something.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.390
Your earnest look made me interested,

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:08.740
I also wanted to give it my all to make a game with everyone.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.780
Did I make such an expression?

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:17.380
I was thinking about how to punish the scenario writer who went crazy last night.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.370
Went crazy?

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.740
She called me in the middle of the night

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:24.630
saying we should put a hidden boss in the demo right then.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:28.570
I just thought, what if a hardcore player came by, you know?

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.280
I just thought the difficulty wouldn't be enough.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:36.390
My only job is tuning the AI difficulty, so I thought I could manage it somehow.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:41.680
However, the person who brought it up was playing other games.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:46.260
You see, I wasn't just having fun, I was playing old RPG games for research!

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:49.310
She seems a bit scary when she gets angry.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:50.980
When did you get to sleep?

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:52.080
Five a.m.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:57.310
A-as you just learned, I'm Seki Ayame, second year student in charge of the scenario.

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:58.600
I'm also a second year student.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.700
I'm Fujikawa Kayo, I'm in charge of the music and sound effects.

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:03.300
Pleased to meet you.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:04.910
You too.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:07.020
What's wrong?

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.940
I just thought you're all amazing people who can do many things.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.630
This club is, um-

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:16.480
Some Dead Fish Eyes, Not Enough Sunlight, Shuttle Run Club.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:19.280
Huh?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.840
There's a reason for the name, but it's a long story.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:30.760
I see.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.640
Now then, about our plans going forward.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:39.770
Last year, thanks to our founder's leadership, we were able to create one puzzle game.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.520
But now, without her, we're basically amateurs.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.680
So we should start with a small project and work our way up.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:51.180
I made a new scenario to show you today.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:54.910
I'll be the leader of the SNS Club's second project!

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.840
Leader? You?

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.880
You sure? Aren't you pushing yourself too hard?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.160
Uh... to hear you say that kinda hurts.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:06.640
I see. You want to make a spin-off of the puzzle game.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:10.220
Y-yes. I thought we could make it into a short visual novel.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.800
I think I could arrange the music we used last time for this.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:14.910
That might be good.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.820
This is exciting, don't you think?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.170
The one who will have to draw the art is you.

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:21.040
Huh? Oh, you're right.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:27.070
I'll have to draw it on a computer, won't I?

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:31.170
Well... if it doesn't seem possible, just say so.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:36.040
You'll have to draw all the sprites, expressions, CGs, and the user interface.

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.200
The creation of all of those items will be entrusted to you.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.450
It's a group project, so there will also be deadlines.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.650
Murakami-san, you don't need to put so much pressure on her.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:50.050
I don't want to pressure her to make something, because making a game is hard.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:55.880
That's right, I'm sure it is hard, and I can't even picture what game art should be like.

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.540
I might not be able to do it.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:00.260
But I...

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.160
I don't want to waste any more time by not having a goal.

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:06.620
I want to create my own game.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:10.140
I'll show you that I can do it!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.280
That's a good reply, Honda-chan.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.380
It'll work out somehow!

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:14.780
Y-yes.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.940
In that case, here's our schedule.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.600
There are many opportunities to sell doujin games,

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.890
but our goal is summer Comiket.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.220
Summer Comiket?

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:29.640
It's an extremely large doujin event during summer vacation.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:34.480
Our current goal is to finish our game and participate in Comiket.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.400
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.180
An impossible schedule would just set us up for failure.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.360
I almost forgot, you can have this.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.710
This is the game you all created, right?

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.900
You don't have to make your art similar.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.750
I think it would be good to make a game that lets you express yourself.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:52.740
Express myself.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.370
All right, I'll think up a new song by tomorrow.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.970
Huh? Is music something that can be made so quickly?

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.210
Is there something I can-

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:02.740
No need to rush! You'll put pressure on me.

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:14.170
Shii, shouldn't you have put it more mildly?

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:18.470
The number of drawings needed from Honda-san is bound to grow.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:22.000
If she ended up collapsing later, I would...

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.810
I know what you mean, but you should be more positive.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:28.740
You were having fun for the first time in a while.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:29.960
I was?

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:32.680
I might have been.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:35.710
It might be because we have a kouhai for the first time.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.970
I'm sure we'll mess up and have setbacks,

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.940
but, with four of us, I think it will work out somehow.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.400
I'll give it my best too, okay, President?

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:49.140
Thanks, Aya, that cheered me up a bit.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:52.680
As thanks, you can have this.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.560
I told you to drink it yourself.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:21.100
Tamaki, are you up late drawing?

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.370
Grandma.

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:24.740
Don't forget to turn off the TV.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:26.900
I will, good night.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.400
What should I do. I feel like I can reproduce it well enough, but...

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:37.860
I think it would be good to make a game that lets you express yourself.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.990
All right, just one more!

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:48.480
I feel that I've finally found what I want to do.

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:25.360
<i>Behold, this dew capped Leontochir!</i>

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:26.440
<i>Stop calling me that.</i>

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:29.020
<i>I wonder if it would be okay to put more old men in.</i>

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.680
<i>I thought our characters would be happy with that too.</i>

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:32.820
<i>It's because it's something you drew, Tama-chan.</i>
